1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,600
In March of 1987, a caretaker in a town of four thousand people reported a car left running.

2
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:09,200
What followed is one of the most badly handled investigations in the county's record.

3
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:13,800
This is a documentary account. Everything here comes from the inquest transcript,

4
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:18,400
the coroner's report, and contemporary reporting in the local paper. Sources are in the description.

5
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:23,000
I am not going to speculate about anyone who was never charged, and I will say when the record is silent.

6
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:27,600
The car belonged to a twenty six year old teaching assistant named in the report as A.M.

7
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:32,100
She had left work at ten past four and was expected at her mother's house by five.

8
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:36,800
The distance is eleven miles. She never arrived, and nobody called it in until the following morning.

9
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:09,700
Here is where the investigation goes wrong, and it goes wrong in the first ninety minutes.

10
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:14,300
The attending officer walked the verge without marking it. Two other officers followed him.

11
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:19,000
By the time a scene of crime officer arrived, three men had walked the same ten metres of mud.

12
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:16,900
According to the coroner's report, and I am going to read this plainly because it matters,

13
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:21,800
the injuries were consistent with a sustained assault with a blunt object, delivered from behind.

14
00:06:21,900 --> 00:06:26,500
The report records seven distinct impact sites, and notes defensive injuries to both forearms.

15
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:31,200
The pathologist concluded she was alive for some minutes after the first blow.

16
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:36,000
I am reading this because the defence later argued the injuries were consistent with a fall,

17
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:41,500
and the jury was never shown the paragraph you just heard. That is the whole point of this episode.

18
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:48,700
The first suspect was a man who had been drinking in the pub at the end of Hollow Lane.

19
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:53,300
He was interviewed four times without a solicitor present, which was irregular even in 1987.

20
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:58,000
He was released without charge and died in 2003. He is not the subject of this video.

21
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:24,600
In 2019 the file was reviewed under the cold case unit and the exhibits were sent for testing.

22
00:11:24,700 --> 00:11:29,200
Two of the seventeen original exhibits could be located. The rest are recorded as destroyed.

23
00:11:29,300 --> 00:11:34,000
Nobody has ever been charged. The inquest verdict remains unlawful killing.

24
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:06,800
If you knew anything about the events on Hollow Lane in March 1987, the number is on screen.

25
00:14:06,900 --> 00:14:11,400
It is a live line. It is still an open case, and forty years is not too late.

26
00:14:11,500 --> 00:14:15,000
Sources, the inquest transcript and the 2019 review, are linked below.
